Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:13:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: offer only H.264 decode on MFC v15
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On the Pixel 7's MFC v15.6 only H.264 has been made to work. The
firmware refuses to open an instance for MPEG-1, MPEG-2, MPEG-4, H.263,
VP8 and VP9 (OPEN_INSTANCE returns error 0x35, then REQBUFS fails with
EIO), and HEVC opens but every frame comes back with a decode error.
Each was tried with FFmpeg's *_v4l2m2m decoder on a short clip.

Advertising them anyway breaks playback: GStreamer ranks its V4L2
decoders above the software ones, picks v4l2vp9dec for a VP9 file, and
the pipeline fails instead of falling back to vp9dec. Leave every
compressed format but H.264 out of the v15 list, H.264 MVC included,
which wasn't tried.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ángel René <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c    | 22 +++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
index 653f7efa6..d26bafe4d 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
@@ -84,7 +84,7 @@ static const struct s5p_mfc_fmt formats[] = {
 		.codec_mode	= S5P_MFC_CODEC_H264_MVC_DEC,
